          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No, and adding one is a common cause of failed floors. Stacking a second compressible layer lets rigid planks flex more than the locking joints tolerate, which works the edges until they gap or crack. Most warranties void explicitly for this. Over concrete you still need a vapour barrier, but that is a thin film, not a cushion.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How thick should vinyl plank underlayment be?",
